From: Hyunho Song <songhh06101@gmail.com>
Subject: ipc/msg: serialize receive permission checks with IPC_SET
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:37:35 -0800

do_msgrcv() checks read permission before taking the queue lock. IPC_SET
can revoke access after that check and before the receiver joins
q_receivers. It then misses the IPC_SET wakeup and can receive a later
message despite losing access.

Take the queue lock before checking read permission and hold it through
each retry after an -EAGAIN wakeup. This also avoids the back-to-back
unlock and relock in the previous revision [1]. The receiver still
drops the lock before sleeping and reacquires it when it must remove
itself from q_receivers.

Signed-off-by: Hyunho Song <songhh06101@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20261120153224.ea4b38665ac135a27f85c652@linux-foundation.org [1]
Reported-by: Hyunho Song <songhh06101@gmail.com>
Closes: https://lore.kernel.org/r/CAJ5=Bnt42P4J_t_4=hUSsAd-WWNSoxendooYm8aTLFjyZqAh=Q@mail.gmail.com
Suggested-by: Manfred Spraul <manfred@colorfullife.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/2f817237-9571-4c06-a7ca-6de93613bb14@colorfullife.com
Cc: Davidlohr Bueso <dave@stgolabs.net>
Cc: <stable@vger.kernel.org>

 ipc/msg.c |    7 ++-----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/ipc/msg.c~ipc-msg-serialize-receive-permission-checks-with-ipc_set
+++ a/ipc/msg.c
@@ -1132,14 +1132,13 @@ static long do_msgrcv(int msqid, void __
 		return PTR_ERR(msq);
 	}
 
+	ipc_lock_object(&msq->q_perm);
 	for (;;) {
 		struct msg_receiver msr_d;
 
 		msg = ERR_PTR(-EACCES);
 		if (ipcperms(ns, &msq->q_perm, S_IRUGO))
-			goto out_unlock1;
-
-		ipc_lock_object(&msq->q_perm);
+			goto out_unlock0;
 
 		/* raced with RMID? */
 		if (!ipc_valid_object(&msq->q_perm)) {
@@ -1248,8 +1247,6 @@ static long do_msgrcv(int msqid, void __
 			msg = ERR_PTR(-ERESTARTNOHAND);
 			goto out_unlock0;
 		}
-
-		ipc_unlock_object(&msq->q_perm);
 	}
 
 out_unlock0:
_
